#disc(titolo: [Adapting Communication to DISC Profiles], profili: (
  (lettera: "D", nome: [Dominance], corpo: [
#strong[Main motivator: decisions and terms];.

With a Dominance\-style patient, I would avoid a lengthy review of the past and get to the point quickly:

#battuta-disc[#emph[“I’ve reassessed the situation, and these are our options today. We can bring part of the original treatment back on track under these terms or, if necessary, replan the case entirely. I’ll explain the differences, and we can decide how to proceed.”];]

If there is a new charge: #emph[“The charge isn’t because you missed appointments. It’s for the work we need to do from today onward to achieve the outcome.”];
  ]),
  (lettera: "I", nome: [Influence], corpo: [
#leva[Main motivator: the future and the outcome.]

With an Influence\-style patient, I would avoid letting the conversation become a long review of everything they failed to do. I can use their willingness to start again to turn their attention immediately to the future:

#battuta-disc[#emph[“Great, then let’s look ahead. Let’s see what we can build on, what we need to redo, and how best to organize this new phase.”];]

The substance of the decision does not change, including any financial terms, but the communication focuses primarily on the outcome.
  ]),
  (lettera: "S", nome: [Steadiness], corpo: [
#leva[Main motivator: reassurance and clarity.]

A Steadiness\-style patient may arrive already worried about being scolded or having to start over from scratch:

#battuta-disc[#emph[“First, let’s take a careful look at where we stand today and how much of what we did can still be brought back on track. Then I’ll explain our options and the terms under which we can restart.”];]

The goal is to reassure the patient about the process without making promises we cannot yet keep.
  ]),
  (lettera: "C", nome: [Conscientiousness], corpo: [
#leva[Main motivator: data and criteria.]

With a Conscientiousness\-style patient, I would make greater use of the available records:

#battuta-disc[#emph[“This was the situation when we stopped, this is where we stand today, and this is the work we still need to do. That is why I can bring this part of the original treatment back on track, while this other part needs to be replanned.”];]
  ]),
))

