With a #strong[D]; patient, I tend to be direct and focused on the decision: “We’ve achieved the goals we set. We can try to change this detail further, but I don’t consider another refinement necessary. If you still want to continue, we can consider it as an additional phase.”
  ]),
  (lettera: "I", nome: [Influence], corpo: [
With an #strong[I]; patient, I focus more on the overall change and social esthetics: “Look how much your smile has changed since we started. The detail you’re showing me is real, but before we continue, I’d like us to consider how important it really is compared with the overall result we’ve achieved.”
  ]),
  (lettera: "S", nome: [Steadiness], corpo: [
With an #strong[S]; patient, I try above all to avoid making the end of treatment feel like abandoning something unfinished: “We’ve achieved the goals we set, and I think it’s right to end treatment here. If this detail remains very important to you, we can still consider it, but it’s not something I think needs correcting.”
  ]),
