#protocollo(capitolo: "16", titolo: [Protocol at a Glance], campi: (
  (etichetta: [When to Use It], corpo: [
#testo-box[When treatment has stalled and we need to decide whether to continue, change methods, or end treatment.]
  ]),
  (etichetta: [Goal], corpo: [
#testo-box[Make a clinically appropriate decision and ensure continuity of care.]
  ]),
  (etichetta: [What to Do], corpo: [
#passi-reset()
#passo[Reassess the treatment plan, clinical response, and adherence, distinguishing temporary difficulties from persistent behaviors.]
#passo[Confirm that the instructions are clear and consistent across the entire team.]
#passo[When indicated, agree on a recovery window that defines the required behaviors, its duration, criteria for assessing progress, and alternatives.]
#passo[Assess change through fit and the movement achieved: a new promise is not enough.]
#passo[Continue if conditions improve; consider another method if the remaining goals are still clinically appropriate; end treatment when appropriate, accepting only clinically sound compromises.]
#passo[Document the goals achieved and those still unmet, the alternatives, and the patient’s choice; clarify any additional costs.]
#passo[If ending treatment, remove the active\-treatment components, provide a retainer, and schedule checkups. In cases of insufficient adherence, the protocol calls for moving directly to retention, without a stabilization phase.]
#passo[Make sure team appointments and communications reflect the decision.]
  ]),
